Oracle Interview Questions — Round 1 & 2 🚀
#OracleInterview

After sharing my Oracle interview journey earlier, I received a lot of messages asking for the actual technical questions that were asked so here are all the questions from Round 1 & Round 2 👇

Round 1 – Screening / Coding Round (on HackerRank)

Q1 – Bash Script
Suppose you have a folder where multiple files are stored.
Write a bash script to check each file and show the highest file size with file name.
Q2 – Jenkins CI/CD Pipeline
Write a Jenkins CI/CD pipeline that you are using in your current project
from code checkout, build, test, deploy, and at last, show the success or failure of the pipeline, and perform cleanup.
Q3 – Kubernetes Manifest
Write a Kubernetes manifest file that uses both Liveness and Readiness probes for health checks.

Round 2 – Technical + Coding + DevOps/SRE Discussion (1 hour 20 mins)
Python
Suppose in a class, many students are appearing for an exam with 5 subjects.  Write a Python script to find the highest marks in each subject along with the student’s name.

Jenkins
How can you run your Jenkins pipeline jobs in parallel?
Jenkins pipelines need to trigger across multi-cloud environments, how would you design this?
How would you implement compliance checks in Jenkins pipelines?
How do you handle cross-region or multi-datacenter deployments using Jenkins?

Kubernetes
How do you ensure deployments roll back automatically if new pods fail?
You need to replicate Kubernetes secrets across multiple clusters, how do you manage this securely?
What’s the difference between ImagePullBackOff and CrashLoopBackOff errors? How do you troubleshoot them?
In a large cluster with hundreds of microservices, how do you ensure observability and control for service-to-service communication?

Docker
Write a Docker Compose file and explain it line by line.
How would you securely expose a containerized API over HTTPS?
How would you ensure all Docker images are scanned for vulnerabilities before deployment?
How do you handle data migration when upgrading containerized databases?

Terraform
How do you secure Terraform state that contains sensitive data?
You need to migrate 100+ existing resources into Terraform, how do you plan this?
How do you design multi-cloud DR using Terraform?
Your Terraform apply is slow due to thousands of resources, how do you optimize it?
Your Terraform apply succeeded, but some resources aren’t behaving as expected, how do you debug this?

SRE Concepts
What do you understand by SRE and explain SLOs, SLIs, and SLAs and also explain error budget.
How do you perform a postmortem after resolving an incident?
How do you handle a P1 incident? Explain your end-to-end steps.


Oracle Interview Experience (3rd & 4th Rounds) — System Design, Managerial & Behavioral 

After completing the first two rounds (Coding + Technical Deep Dive), the next stages focused on System Design, SRE mindset, and Managerial capabilities — these were truly challenging and insightful!

3rd Round — System Design (1 hour)
This round focused deeply on scalability, reliability, fault tolerance, and architecture design using AWS, Kubernetes, Terraform, and CI/CD best practices.

Key Topics & Questions Asked:

Design a highly available and fault-tolerant web application architecture using AWS.
Explain how load balancing, auto scaling, and multi-AZ setup ensure reliability.
How would you design a zero-downtime deployment strategy (Rolling vs Blue/Green vs Canary)?
How do you manage stateful services in Kubernetes?
Design an observability stack (Prometheus + Grafana + Alertmanager).
How do you perform capacity planning for a growing system?
How to handle database failover and replication in AWS RDS?
Design a CI/CD pipeline integrating Terraform, Jenkins, Docker, and K8s.
How do you ensure cost optimization in a large distributed system?
Explain how you would ensure disaster recovery (RTO/RPO) for critical systems.
How do you handle cross-region deployments in Jenkins or Harness?
Design a secure CI/CD pipeline with pre-deployment approvals and rollback mechanisms.
How do you handle config drift between environments (dev, stage, prod)?

They mainly checked the thought process, trade-offs, and real-world SRE experience.

4th Round — Managerial + Behavioral (1:10 hours)

This round was focused on team culture, leadership attitude, ownership, and problem-solving mindset.

Tell me about a production incident (P1) you handled — what steps did you take?
How do you prioritize issues when multiple systems are impacted?
Describe a time you disagreed with a manager or senior — how did you handle it?
How do you ensure collaboration between Dev and Ops teams?
What’s your approach to automation — what kind of manual tasks have you automated recently?
How do you handle stress or pressure during outages?
How do you perform and document Root Cause Analysis (RCA)?
How do you ensure reliability, observability, and performance in production?
What kind of work culture helps you perform at your best?
Why Oracle?
Tell me about a failed deployment — how did you troubleshoot and prevent it from happening again?
How do you manage time and prioritize tasks under pressure?
How do you ensure your team follows DevOps best practices consistently?
What motivates you most about SRE work — reliability, automation, or problem-solving?

Overall Takeaway
Each round was a new learning experience — it pushed me to think like an SRE who not only builds but also owns and optimizes systems.



Final Round Interview at  Oracle – Hiring Manager Round 🚀

The Hiring Manager round was a deep dive discussion that focused not only on my technical expertise but also on my approach to ownership, communication, leadership, and handling critical production challenges.

Here are some of the questions that were asked in this round 👇

Can you walk me through your most recent project architecture — what was your exact contribution and impact?
How do you prioritize incidents or production issues when multiple systems are affected?
Tell me about a major P1 incident you handled — what caused it, how you resolved it, and what preventive actions you implemented later?
How do you ensure zero-downtime deployment for critical production services?
How do you collaborate with Development, QA, and SRE/Operations teams during release cycles?
What’s your approach to improving overall system reliability and reducing MTTR?
How do you ensure security, compliance, and governance in your CI/CD pipelines (Jenkins or Harness)?
Can you explain how you designed a fault-tolerant and highly available infrastructure in AWS or multi-cloud environments?
Describe a situation where you had to make a tough technical decision under pressure — how did you balance trade-offs?
Tell me about a time your automation or deployment failed — how did you handle the rollback and what did you learn?
How do you measure service performance and reliability — what SLIs, SLOs, and SLAs do you track?
What’s your incident response strategy — from alert to RCA (Root Cause Analysis)?
How do you ensure observability and proactive issue detection across microservices?
What automation have you recently implemented that significantly improved productivity or reliability?
How do you handle disagreements or conflicts within your team or with other stakeholders?
What’s your approach to mentoring or guiding junior engineers in the team?
How do you balance innovation, reliability, and security while managing critical systems?
Why do you want to join Oracle, and how do you see yourself contributing in the next few years?

This round was a perfect blend of technical depth and behavioral insight — more like a discussion to understand not just what I do, but how I think, decide, and lead during challenges.

I’m truly thankful to the Oracle interview panel and HR team for such a smooth and insightful interview journey across all rounds.

Key Takeaway:
Technical excellence gets you through the door, but your mindset, clarity, and collaboration keep you in the room. 💪
